A||N||4||PKFieroGT||Short Shifter and grinding into third||||5||
Z||000000||PKFieroGT||05-01-2001||09:02 AM||||Hello all,<BR>Sorry about the new thread, but my problem has me concerned.I just installed a short shifter into my 86 GT 2.8 4spd, and it was like driving in heaven!! Short throws, quick shifts and I can rest my whole arm on the console as i drive!!! BUT...<BR>Just recently (yesterday) I noticed that eveytime I shift into third (either from second to third, or fourth to third) I get that infamous grind/clunk outta the tranny, like the syncros messed up. This only happens in third, no other gear. This leads me to believe it may have something to do with my Short install, 'cause this never happened before. I have several options and need feedback on which it may be;<BR>1) problem with the Hydraulics<BR>2)bad tranny  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>3) When I removed the cable from the old<BR>shifter, ther is a little metal clip that fits over the end of the shifter cable(where the cotter pin holds it in). Well this thing flew off and dropped down below into the cavity below the shifter, and I haven't replaced it. I just stuck the cable on hoping it would be ok. I have a feeling that it isn't!<BR>Any thoughts rants or raves?<BR>Thanks!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||05-01-2001||03:04 PM||||Rant.  Rave.  There.  And I've never really had a thought.  What's that like?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>My first guess would be that the shift cable (the fore-and-aft motion transmitter cable) has a little slop in it.  The little thingy-bopper-whatsit that popped off probably wants to be there.  Look for it in the car, nab it with a telescoping magnet or something.  If you can't find it in the car, get one from salvage yard (probably doesn't have to be from a Fiero - just a GM front-wheel-drive with manual shift?).  Or, call a GM dealership and ask.  Even if it costs a buck, it's a cheap fix  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>||||reg||12
Z||000002||jaguiler||05-01-2001||10:49 PM||||read your review....I'm getting a short shifter too.... soon.....have to decide where to oder from $$$<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||05-01-2001||11:58 PM||||I'm having the same problem intermittently even with a newly rebuilt transmission, again like you - with the 3rd gear only.  I tried adjusting the cables at the trans end without making any difference.  I suspect there is some wear somewhere, either at the transmission end shifter arm or perhaps the mechanism under the shifter.  Rodney Dickman has a rebuild kit for the trans shifter arm.  I'm going to try that and hope that solves the problem.  Anyone else had this problem that they managed to solve?? ||||reg||10
Z||000004||PKFieroGT||05-02-2001||08:38 AM||||Thanks eveyone,<P>I suspect it is that thinga-ma-bob thingy that the cable attaches to the shifter arm, because I never had this problem before I installed the arm. Once I replace it (tried to look for it yesterday and it was nowhere to be found)I'll post a topic to let you know of my findings...<P>Again .... THANKS!!!<P>Petri||||reg||7
